<title>GERMANY: German Adtranz wins intercity train deal.</title>
<headline>German Adtranz wins intercity train deal.</headline>
<dateline>HENNINGSDORF, Germany 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Adtranz, the railways joint venture of ABB Ltd and Daimler Benz AG, said on Thursday it had won a contract to supply control systems for 35 German intercity trains.</p>
<p>The contract given by Weiden-based Partner fuer Fahrzeugausstattung (PFA) is worth around 24 million marks, Adtranz said in a statement.</p>
<p>Adtranz said it would co-operate on the contract with Linke Hofmann Busch and LZB, a consortium of Siemens AG and Alcatel SEL.</p>
<p>The first vehicles are to be delivered in May 1997.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
